# Pinia Colada

**Language:** Write all query definitions, API helpers, comments, and related commit messages in **English**.

[Pinia Colada](https://pinia-colada.esm.dev/) (`@pinia/colada`) handles **read-heavy, cacheable server data**. It complements — but does not replace — Pinia setup stores in `ui/src/stores/`. See `.cursor/rules/pinia-stores.mdc` for mutable domain state.

Registered in `ui/src/main.ts`: `app.use(createPinia())` then `app.use(PiniaColada)`.

## Official documentation

When unsure about Colada APIs, caching, query keys, or mutations, **check the official docs first** before guessing:

- [Pinia Colada documentation](https://pinia-colada.esm.dev/)

Useful entry points:

- [Queries](https://pinia-colada.esm.dev/guide/query.html)
- [Query keys](https://pinia-colada.esm.dev/guide/query-keys.html)
- [defineQueryOptions](https://pinia-colada.esm.dev/guide/query-options.html)

Prefer documented Colada patterns over ad-hoc caching in Pinia stores. If the docs and this repo diverge, follow **this project's conventions** below and align with `vehicle-configurator.queries.ts`.

## When to use Colada vs Pinia stores

| Use **Colada** (`ui/src/queries/`)            | Use **Pinia store** (`ui/src/stores/`)  |
| --------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| GET-style reads that benefit from cache/dedup | Selected entity, wizard state, UI flags |
| Shared lists/options keyed by request params  | Mutations, POST/PATCH flows             |
| Multiple components need the same cached read | Loader/dialog flags (`loader.store`)    |

**Do not** migrate legacy store domains to Colada unless explicitly asked. **Do not** grow an existing store with large read-only caches — add a query in `ui/src/queries/` instead.

## File layout

| Path                                 | Role                                      |
| ------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |
| `ui/src/queries/{domain}.queries.ts` | `defineQueryOptions`, query key factories |
| `ui/src/queries/index.ts`            | Barrel exports                            |
| `ui/src/api/{domain}.api.ts`         | Thin HTTP functions used by queries       |

Reference implementation: `vehicle-configurator.queries.ts` + `vehicle-configurator.api.ts`.

## Naming (project convention)

| Item                 | Pattern                        | Example                                |
| -------------------- | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------- |
| Query file           | `{domain}.queries.ts`          | `vehicle-configurator.queries.ts`      |
| API helper file      | `{domain}.api.ts`              | `vehicle-configurator.api.ts`          |
| Key factory          | `{DOMAIN}_KEYS`                | `VEHICLE_CONFIGURATOR_KEYS`            |
| Query options export | `{domain}{Resource}` camelCase | `vehicleConfiguratorRegulatedProducts` |

## Query definitions (`defineQueryOptions`)

- Export named query options from `*.queries.ts`
- Use a **key factory** object for stable, hierarchical keys
- Include every parameter that affects the response in the key
- Set `enabled` when required params are missing — do not fire invalid requests
- Keep `query` thin: call `@/api/` helpers, not raw HTTP inside the query file

See also `.cursor/rules/services.mdc` for `services/` vs `api/` boundaries.

```ts
import { defineQueryOptions } from '@pinia/colada';
import { getMyDomainItems } from '@/api';

export const MY_KEYS = {
  root: ['my-domain'] as const,
  items: (payload: PayloadInterface) => [...MY_KEYS.root, 'items', payload.id ?? ''] as const,
};

const hasRequiredPayload = (payload: PayloadInterface) => Boolean(payload?.id);

export const myDomainItems = defineQueryOptions((payload: PayloadInterface) => ({
  key: MY_KEYS.items(payload),
  enabled: hasRequiredPayload(payload),
  query: async () => getMyDomainItems(payload),
}));
```

## Consuming queries in components

- `import { useQuery } from '@pinia/colada'`
- Import query options from `@/queries`
- Pass a **getter** so the query reacts to param changes

```ts
const productsPayload = computed(() => ({
  /* params */
}));

const regulatedProducts = useQuery(() => vehicleConfiguratorRegulatedProducts(productsPayload.value));
```

- Use `.data`, `.isPending`, `.error`, and `.refresh` — match `SupplementaryProductsSection.vue`

## API helpers (`ui/src/api/`)

- One function per endpoint; return unwrapped response data
- Use `UiApiUrlPathEnum` for paths
- Class services in `@/services/` remain the default for non-Colada flows; Colada queries import from `@/api`

## Inline `useQuery` inside stores

A rare hybrid exists (e.g. `customer-offer.store.ts`). **Prefer** `ui/src/queries/` for new reusable reads. Only colocate `useQuery` in a store when the query is tightly coupled to that store and not reused elsewhere.

## Before finishing

- [ ] Query keys include all response-affecting parameters
- [ ] `enabled` guards missing or invalid params
- [ ] HTTP lives in `ui/src/api/` (or an existing service) — not duplicated
- [ ] New queries exported from `ui/src/queries/index.ts`
- [ ] Components use `useQuery(() => ...)` for reactive params
- [ ] Did not refactor unrelated Pinia stores to Colada
